[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3314633817","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110717#issuecomment-3314633817","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110717","id":3314633817,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7FkUxZ","user":{"login":"Shadows-of-Fire","id":3682588,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2ODI1ODg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3682588?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire","html_url":"https://github.com/Shadows-of-Fire","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-20T06:33:49Z","updated_at":"2025-09-20T06:33:49Z","body":"The error messages in the tests that appear to be impacted from this change are surprisingly unhelpful. It seems like `utils.notest.gd::check(condition)` is unable to actually print a backtrace, and only produces `Check failed. Backtrace (most recent call first):`.\r\n\r\nGoing to have to fiddle around to see why, I guess.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3314633817/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3314639386","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110717#issuecomment-3314639386","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110717","id":3314639386,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7FkWIa","user":{"login":"Shadows-of-Fire","id":3682588,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2ODI1ODg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3682588?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire","html_url":"https://github.com/Shadows-of-Fire","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-20T06:40:16Z","updated_at":"2025-09-20T06:40:16Z","body":"Okay, had to find/replace uses of `Utils.check` in the failing tests with `assert` (seemed to be the fastest way to get line data without fighting `check`).\r\n\r\nOne of the failing tests is this hunk from `typed_dictionary_usage.gd`:\r\n```\r\n\tvar typed_int := 556\r\n\tvar converted_floats: Dictionary[float, float] = { typed_int: typed_int }\r\n\tconverted_floats[498.0] = 894\r\n\tassert(str(converted_floats) == '{ 556.0: 556.0, 498.0: 894.0 }')\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis fails because of this deviation:  \r\n```\r\nreal:      { 556.0: 556, 498.0: 894.0 }\r\nexpected:  { 556.0: 556.0, 498.0: 894.0 }\r\n```\r\nNote the missing `.0` for the value `556`. Does this imply that when using initializer-list syntax with `set_typed` that the _keys_ are converted but not the values?\r\n\r\nOr is this some kind of floating-point printing error","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3314639386/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3314644643","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110717#issuecomment-3314644643","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110717","id":3314644643,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7FkXaj","user":{"login":"Shadows-of-Fire","id":3682588,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2ODI1ODg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3682588?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire","html_url":"https://github.com/Shadows-of-Fire","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-20T06:46:23Z","updated_at":"2025-09-20T06:46:23Z","body":"Well, I guess that answers my question, lol\r\n```\r\n// WARNING: This operator does not validate the value type. For scripting/extensions this is\r\n// done in `variant_setget.cpp`. Consider using `set()` if the data might be invalid.\r\nVariant &Dictionary::operator[](const Variant &p_key) {\r\n```\r\n\r\nGuessing the case is the same for `Array` then.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3314644643/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3314658869","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110717#issuecomment-3314658869","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110717","id":3314658869,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Fka41","user":{"login":"Shadows-of-Fire","id":3682588,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2ODI1ODg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3682588?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire","html_url":"https://github.com/Shadows-of-Fire","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-20T06:55:37Z","updated_at":"2025-09-20T07:10:41Z","body":"Well, at least for the dictionary case, using `Dictionary::set` seems to handle it. The perf is a little bit worse than `operator[]`, but still substantially better than the copy case.\r\n\r\nFrom the benchmark in #110709 (but without the `reserve()` changes) - \r\n\r\n```\r\nTime with `set_typed` and `set` (this change after last commit)\r\ntime untyped: 17660ms\r\ntime typed: 19050ms\r\n\r\nTime with copy and `operator[]` (before this change)\r\ntime untyped: 17533ms\r\ntime typed: 45386ms\r\n```","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3314658869/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3315459852","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110717#issuecomment-3315459852","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110717","id":3315459852,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7FnecM","user":{"login":"Shadows-of-Fire","id":3682588,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2ODI1ODg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3682588?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire","html_url":"https://github.com/Shadows-of-Fire","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Shadows-of-Fire/received_ev